<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  GalacticEmpire_Campaign.xml            UtinniPatches · split 2026-11-07
  ============================================================================

  The Ash'karr campaign's half of the Galactic Empire, builds FACTION_SPEC.md
  section 1 under V1_CHAIN R15. The reskin every Star Wars game wants (name,
  title, favor word and icon, troopers' word, faction badge, the Rising Order)
  moved to RimStarWars on the owner's word of 2026-11-07, in
  `src/RimStarWars/StarWarsPatches/Patches/GalacticEmpire.xml`; it runs first
  (this mod loads after mandrake.rsw.patches), but nothing here relies on it.

  What stays here names this campaign: the RUT_ leader and raid kinds, the RUT_
  culture, the whitelist of this world's factions, the hostility to the player
  (Pillar 5), this world's settlement count and the description of this world.

  It patches VANILLA `Empire` (Royalty). R15's reason is
  `settlementGenerationWeight`: the occupier has to outweigh the locals to read
  as one.

  ⚠️ It still references `OuterRim_Imp*` PAWN KINDS under MayRequire, so the
  Neronix17.OuterRim.GalacticEmpire dependency stays. The Outer Rim FACTION def
  is no longer touched.

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEF, game up, 2026-08-14 - not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Royalty\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Faction_Empire.xml

      settlementGenerationWeight  1
      techLevel                   Ultra
      permanentEnemy              ABSENT      -> Add, not Replace
      fixedLeaderKinds            WRITTEN (line 90) -> Replace, not Add
      pawnGroupMakers             [1] Trader · [2] Combat commonality 100 ·
                                  [3] Combat commonality 10 · [4] Settlement

  ⚠️ techLevel is left alone. The spec's "Spacer (vessel default)" mis-reads the
  vessel - it actually ships `Ultra` - but the instruction is "no change", so
  no change is what this file makes.

  🔑 THE COMBAT GROUPS ARE NAMED BY THEIR COMMONALITY, NOT BY POSITION. A positional
  predicate would be correct today and wrong the moment any mod inserts a group ahead
  of ours; `[commonality="100"]` cannot drift. It is also the form both engines agree
  on — ElementTree's `[N]` counts siblings by tag while XPath 1.0's counts the nodes
  the previous predicate kept, so `li[kindDef="Combat"][1]` reads as DEAD under a
  findall()-based checker while RimWorld's System.Xml resolves it correctly.

  ⛔ COMBAT GROUPS ONLY. `pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"]` is TWO nodes on
  this def, so each op carries a positional predicate on the filtered set. The
  Trader and Settlement groups are untouched by design: they carry the
  Royalty trade and settlement pawns, which are not part of R15.

  🔑 THE RAID IS OURS NOW — IMPERIAL_RAID_ROSTER_1, 2026-08-21. Both combat
  groups were built out of Outer Rim's `OuterRim_ImpStorm*` line troops, and the
  four Imperial kinds this mod authors in
  `Defs/PawnKindDefs/JawaFactionRoster.xml` had NO SPAWN ROUTE AT ALL:
  `defaultFactionDef` names the faction a kind belongs to, it does not put the
  kind in a raid. Only a `pawnGroupMaker` does. So the three fighting kinds now
  carry both groups:

      RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt        5      stormtrooper,     combatPower  87
      RUT_Jawa_Empire_Heavy        2      heavy trooper,    combatPower 129
      RUT_Jawa_Empire_Specialist   1.5    Imperial officer, combatPower 119

  and the fourth, `RUT_Jawa_Empire_Leader` (Emperor Palpatine, combatPower 211), is
  wired in through `fixedLeaderKinds` above rather than through a group, because
  a leader is generated once for the faction and not rolled into raids.

  The three Outer Rim SPECIALISTS stay in the RARE group only
  (`OuterRim_ImpRangeTrooper`, `_ImpDeathTrooper`, `_ImpISBAgent`, all
  combatPower 200), mirroring vanilla's own split where the commonality-10 group
  carries the heavier option list. They are kept because they are flavour the
  authored four do not carry. None of them holds the 99999 exclude-from-raid
  sentinel; checked, all three are 200.

  ⚠️ Our three kinds stay INSIDE the Outer Rim `PatchOperationFindMod` even
  though they are ours, and that is deliberate: `RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt` declares
  `apparelRequired` on `OuterRim_StormtrooperCuirass` and
  `OuterRim_StormtrooperHelmet`, so without that mod the whole group is wrong
  anyway.

  ⛔ Do NOT touch the Trader or Settlement groups. They keep Royalty's villagers,
  janissaries and cataphracts by design === FACTION_SPEC.md:130, EMPIRE_GAP_AUDIT.md
  section 3.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Everything is inside a conditional on the Empire def existing, so the file is
  a silent no-op without Royalty rather than a wall of red. The group-maker ops
  additionally sit inside a `PatchOperationFindMod` for Outer Rim - Galactic
  Empire, and every Imperial defName also carries `MayRequire`, because an
  unwrapped defName from a disabled mod is a silent no-op that reads as success.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!--
          The leader the world actually names. WRITTEN on the vessel
          (Data/Royalty/Defs/FactionDefs/Faction_Empire.xml:90, one li holding
          Empire_Royal_Stellarch), so this is a REPLACE. An Add here would
          append a second li and the Stellarch would keep rolling half the time.

          OUTSIDE the Outer Rim FindMod on purpose: RUT_Jawa_Empire_Leader is ours,
          shipped in this same mod, and needs no third-party gate.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/fixedLeaderKinds</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedLeaderKinds>
              <li>RUT_Jawa_Empire_Leader</li>
            </fixedLeaderKinds>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>The occupier, and the only permanent enemy. Not hateful — procedural. Standardised infantry moved by drop-pod, security droids that were requisitioned rather than chosen, the rare Sith attached to nothing anyone can name, and a reach that is mostly orbital.\n\nIt does not want this world. It wants what leaves this world on schedule.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          Pillar 5: the Galactic Empire alone is the permanent enemy - but it is
          permanently hostile to a NAMED SET, not to the whole planet.
          Owner's ruling 2026-08-20, "Option (b) please";
          design/Jawa/worldbuilding/EMPIRE_GAP_AUDIT.md section 2 carries the
          reasoning for every entry.

          permanentEnemy is set FALSE rather than removed, and that is not a
          style choice. FactionDef.PermanentlyHostileTo tests it FIRST:

              if (permanentEnemy) return true;
              if (permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept != null
                  && !permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept.Contains(otherFactionDef))
                  return true;

          so leaving it true returns before the list is ever read and makes the
          whole whitelist dead code. ABSENT on the vessel, so this is an Add.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]</xpath>
          <value><permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy></value>
        </li>

        <!--
          THE WHITELIST, and read the direction before editing it: this lists who
          is NOT a permanent enemy. Anything absent from it IS one.

          PRESENT on the vessel (Faction_Empire.xml line 57), so this is a
          Replace, not an Add.

          The shipped list carries PlayerTribe and PlayerColony. Both are
          DELIBERATELY DROPPED here, and that single omission is what keeps the
          Empire permanently hostile to the player - the owner's 2026-08-14
          ruling. Also dropped, also deliberately: RUT_Jawa_FreeDroidEnclaves,
          RUT_Jawa_GeonosianFoundryHive, RUT_Jawa_WildsteamClan and RUT_Jawa_AscendantHelix.
          Do not "helpfully" restore any of the six.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept</xpath>
          <value>
            <permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept>
              <li>RUT_Jawa_HuttCartel</li>
              <li>RUT_Jawa_DeepwaterCompact</li>
              <li>RUT_Jawa_IndigenousTribes</li>
              <li>RUT_Jawa_Junkers</li>
              <li>OutlanderCivil</li>
              <li>TribeCivil</li>
              <li>Pirate</li>
              <li>Ancients</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Beggars</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">ResearchExpedition</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">GravshipCrew</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">TradersGuild</li>
            </permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- 1 -> 0.45. Three surface settlements by design; the other seven or
             eight are orbital fiction the map never has to draw. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/settlementGenerationWeight</xpath>
          <value><settlementGenerationWeight>0.45</settlementGenerationWeight></value>
        </li>

        <!-- R15: stormtroopers, not cataphracts. Combat groups only. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
          <mods>
            <li>Outer Rim - Galactic Empire</li>
          </mods>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>

              <!-- The common raid (vanilla commonality 100). Line troops, plus
                   the attack droids beside them.

                   ═══ DROID_FACTION_LOADOUTS_1 (packet C1), 2026-09-08 ═══════════
                   Ruling 2, verbatim: "The Empire will use Droids in their attacks.
                   Stormtroopers + Attack Droids working together." The design doc's
                   §3.2 mechanism cell: "DW KotOR Bad + JDS battle kinds at 20-40 %
                   of points; `Jawa_Empire_*` kinds untouched" - and untouched they
                   are, same three defNames at the same three weights as before.

                   🔑 THE SHARE IS OF POINTS, NOT OF PICKS, so the weights are sized
                   against combatPower, not eyeballed. Read off the live 600-mod dump
                   2026-09-08 (RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt 101 / Heavy 129 / Specialist 119 -
                   the Grunt is 101, NOT the 87 this file's own header comment still
                   records from 2026-08-21; the roster generator has been re-run since):

                       organic   5x101 + 2x129 + 1.5x119            =  941.5
                       droids  1.5x120 + 1.5x75 + 1.5x45 + 1x45     =  405.0
                       droid share = 405 / 1346.5                   =  30.1 %

                   which sits in the middle of the ruled 20-40 % band rather than at
                   its ceiling. Ruling 2 is explicit that these armies are still
                   mostly organic troops.

                   ⚠️ RSW_DW_OuterRim_ImperialKXSecurityDroid is the Empire's OWN KX
                   security droid, carried by Droidworks - §2's R3 row already rules
                   it "IS an Empire attack droid now". The JDS Separatist kinds beside
                   it are deliberate and this file's own description sentence licenses
                   them: "security droids that were requisitioned rather than chosen".

                   ⚠️ MayRequire on every droid entry, same reason the OuterRim kinds
                   in the rare group carry one: an unwrapped defName from a disabled
                   mod is a silent no-op that reads as success. -->
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="100"]/options</xpath>
                <value>
                  <options>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt>5</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Heavy>2</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Heavy>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Specialist>1.5</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Specialist>
                    <RSW_DW_OuterRim_ImperialKXSecurityDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1.5</RSW_DW_OuterRim_ImperialKXSecurityDroid>
                    <RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_DevWD_weak MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1.5</RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_DevWD_weak>
                    <RSW_DW_JDSCIS_BX_Commando_Droid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1.5</RSW_DW_JDSCIS_BX_Commando_Droid>
                    <RSW_DW_JDSCIS_B2_Super_Battle_Droid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1</RSW_DW_JDSCIS_B2_Super_Battle_Droid>
                  </options>
                </value>
              </li>

              <!-- The rare raid (vanilla commonality 10). Line troops plus the
                   three 200-power specialists. -->
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="10"]/options</xpath>
                <value>
                  <options>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt>5</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Heavy>2</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Heavy>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Specialist>1.5</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Specialist>
                    <OuterRim_ImpRangeTrooper MayRequire="Neronix17.OuterRim.GalacticEmpire">2</OuterRim_ImpRangeTrooper>
                    <OuterRim_ImpDeathTrooper MayRequire="Neronix17.OuterRim.GalacticEmpire">1.5</OuterRim_ImpDeathTrooper>
                    <OuterRim_ImpISBAgent MayRequire="Neronix17.OuterRim.GalacticEmpire">1</OuterRim_ImpISBAgent>
                    <!-- C1: the heavier droid line, matching this group's own
                         "line troops plus specialists" character. Weighted power
                         1.5x120 + 1x125 + 0.5x150 + 1.5x45 = 447.5 against an
                         organic floor of 941.5 (the three Jawa_Empire_* kinds)
                         BEFORE the three Outer Rim specialists above are counted,
                         so the droid share is at most 32 % and in practice lower -
                         inside the ruled 20-40 % band from the top. -->
                    <RSW_DW_OuterRim_ImperialKXSecurityDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1.5</RSW_DW_OuterRim_ImperialKXSecurityDroid>
                    <RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_SentWD MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1</RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_SentWD>
                    <RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_DevWD_strong MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">0.5</RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_DevWD_strong>
                    <RSW_DW_JDSCIS_BX_Commando_Droid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1.5</RSW_DW_JDSCIS_BX_Commando_Droid>
                  </options>
                </value>
              </li>

              <!-- 🔴 B40's OTHER HALF, added 2026-08-22. R15's comment above says
                   "Combat groups only", and that is exactly what left the SETTLEMENT group
                   untouched. Measured in the live 578-mod dump it still fielded
                   Empire_Fighter_Trooper, _Janissary, _Cataphract and _Champion, five
                   vanilla mech kinds, a Mechanitor and RBM_MinotaurGuardianHigh, at
                   commonality 100.
                   ⇒ B40 took the cataphracts out of the RAIDS and left them defending the
                   Imperial settlement - the half a player is most likely to look at, because
                   he walks onto that map and chooses when to leave it.
                   ⚠️ The options node is replaced WHOLE, so the mech kinds and the modded
                   Minotaur go with the knights. That is deliberate: a settlement of Imperial
                   troops is the point, and vanilla's own four are the ones the item names.
                   🔑 Same three kinds and the same weights as the common raid, so a
                   settlement reads as the same army a raid does. The Leader is not here - he
                   is generated once per faction through fixedLeaderKinds. -->
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Settlement"]/options</xpath>
                <value>
                  <options>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt>5</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Grunt>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Heavy>2</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Heavy>
                    <RUT_Jawa_Empire_Specialist>1.5</RUT_Jawa_Empire_Specialist>
                    <!-- C1: the same four droid entries at the same four weights as
                         the common raid, for the same reason B40 mirrored the troops
                         here - a player walks onto that map and chooses when to
                         leave it, so the settlement must read as the same army the
                         raid does. Droid share 30.1 % of points, identical. -->
                    <RSW_DW_OuterRim_ImperialKXSecurityDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1.5</RSW_DW_OuterRim_ImperialKXSecurityDroid>
                    <RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_DevWD_weak MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1.5</RSW_DW_KotORDroidBad_DevWD_weak>
                    <RSW_DW_JDSCIS_BX_Commando_Droid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1.5</RSW_DW_JDSCIS_BX_Commando_Droid>
                    <RSW_DW_JDSCIS_B2_Super_Battle_Droid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">1</RSW_DW_JDSCIS_B2_Super_Battle_Droid>
                  </options>
                </value>
              </li>

            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ═══ LEADER_TITLES_ON_THE_IDEO_1, 2026-08-22 ═══════════════════════════════
       `Faction.LeaderTitle` (RimWorld/Faction.cs:142) prefers the primary IDEO's
       `leaderTitleMale` and only falls back to `def.leaderTitle`. Measured live:
       the ideo overrode the def on 36 of 37 factions, so the Galactic Empire's authored
       title "Emperor" was never the word a player read. The ideo's title is
       generated from its CULTURE's `leaderTitleMaker`, so the route is a culture
       of our own - full mechanism in `Defs/CultureDefs/JawaLeaderTitles.xml`.
       ⛔ Not a patch on the shared vanilla culture: Sophian is shared with every
       faction of its category in 578 mods and patching it renames all of them.
       ⚠️ This BAKES at world creation and cannot be retrofitted. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/allowedCultures</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/allowedCultures</xpath>
      <value><allowedCultures><li>RUT_Jawa_Culture_Empire</li></allowedCultures></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ═══ EMPIRE_WHITELIST_OVERRIDDEN_1, 2026-08-30 ═══════════════════════════════
       `permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept` (the whitelist, patched above) turns out NOT
       to be the last word on Empire hostility: SWCP_Core (bundled in "Star Wars
       KotOR Resources and Materials") postfixes `FactionDef.PermanentlyHostileTo`
       and three sibling methods (goodwill-situation, goodwill-lock, initial-relation)
       to read a `SWCP.Core.ModExtension_FactionPermanentlyHostileTo` mod extension
       FIRST, additively - it can force hostility TRUE regardless of what the
       whitelist ends up containing, and nothing else in the mod set writes that
       extension, so this cannot lose a patch race the way the whitelist can.
       Live merged Empire def checked 2026-08-30: no existing <modExtensions>, so
       this is a fresh Add of the whole element, not an Add into an existing list.
       ⚠️ Gated on PatchOperationFindMod: a `Class=` naming a type no loaded
       assembly has silently DISCARDS THE WHOLE FactionDef
       (modextension-missing-type-discards-def) - this must no-op if SWCP is cut. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Star Wars KotOR Resources and Materials</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <modExtensions>
          <li Class="SWCP.Core.ModExtension_FactionPermanentlyHostileTo">
            <hostileFactionDefs>
              <li>PlayerColony</li>
              <li>PlayerTribe</li>
            </hostileFactionDefs>
          </li>
        </modExtensions>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>